<description>
Fill every fully enclosed background region inside red outlines with blue.

Input structure
- The grid has a black background and red one-cell-thick outline/barrier pixels.
- Red outlines may touch each other or the grid boundary, and some red shapes
  may be incomplete.
- Blue is absent from the input and appears only as the fill color.

Rule
- Treat red pixels as walls and trace all background pixels connected to the
  grid boundary by 4-neighbor steps.
- Recolor each remaining background pixel to blue.
- Leave red pixels and exterior background unchanged.

Key insight
- The blue cells are exactly the background holes: black regions that cannot
  escape to the outer boundary without crossing a red wall.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "transform_in_place",
  "src": "red 4-connected outline/barrier pixels on black background, with some barriers enclosing background holes",
  "transform": "preserve red pixels; flood-fill border-connected background as background and recolor the remaining enclosed background regions blue"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 8-12 rows x 8-12 cols, always square
  colors: black(0) background, red(2) walls only; blue(1) absent from input, appears only in output
  red_walls:
    structure: 1-cell-thick axis-aligned line segments forming rectangular frames
    no 2x2 red blocks; walls meet at right-angle corners
    frames: 1-3 complete rectangular frames with outer dimensions 4x4 to 5x5 (interior 2x3 to 3x3)
    sharing: when multiple frames exist, all share at least one wall segment with another frame
    red_percentage: 27-41% of grid cells
  isolated_dots: 0-1 isolated red pixel per frame interior (no red 4-neighbors); total 1-3 per grid
  distractor: |
    0-1 open structures per grid: partial rectangular outline sharing walls with frame cluster,
    bounded partly by grid border instead of red walls. Interior connects to border via
    4-neighbor black path so is NOT enclosed. May contain an isolated red dot.
  transform: flood-fill from border through black cells; recolor unreachable black cells blue; red unchanged
  enclosed_regions: 1-3 per grid; each is a rectangular hole inside a complete frame (minus any internal dot)

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Choose grid size N x N, N in [8..12].
    2. Place 1-3 complete rectangular frames (outer 4x5 or 5x5) on the grid, ensuring each shares at least one wall with another. Draw all frame walls as red.
    3. Optionally place 0-1 isolated red dot inside each frame interior (centered or near-center).
    4. Optionally add 1 distractor open structure sharing a wall with the frame cluster, extending toward a grid border with one side missing (border substitutes for wall). May include an isolated red dot.
    5. Verify all frame interiors are flood-fill-enclosed (not reachable from border through black) and distractor interiors are reachable. Fill enclosed black cells with blue to produce the output.
    6. The input is the output with all blue cells replaced by black.
```
